# Every text file is LF, in the repository and in the working tree, on every
# platform -- eol=lf rather than plain text=auto, because a contributor with
# core.autocrlf=true would otherwise check out CRLF and `npm pack` reads the
# WORKING TREE. The release records a SHA-256 for each shipped file, and
# BUILD-INFO.json ties src/nanoepoch.c to the binaries compiled from it, so a
# file that is CRLF here and LF on a Linux runner hashes differently in the two
# places and fails a gate for a reason that has nothing to do with its contents.
#
# It also keeps the shell scripts working: checked out with CRLF they fail
# inside the Linux build containers with "bad interpreter: no such file or
# directory", which is a confusing way to learn about line endings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Compiled addons must never be line-ending converted.
*.node binary
